According to a report by Intel Market Research, Global motor and solenoid drivers market size was valued at USD 2.46 billion in 2025. The market will expand from USD 2.58 billion in 2026 to USD 4.12 billion by 2034, exhibiting a compound annual growth rate of approximately 7.0% during the forecast period.
Reflecting the accelerating pace of innovation and expanding application scope, the CAGR has been refined upward from the prior estimate.
Motor drivers regulate voltage, current and signal inputs for a wide range of electric motors, while solenoid drivers control electromagnetic actuators used in fluid power systems. Both families of integrated circuits enable precise motion control, position holding and rapid switching across sectors such as industrial automation, robotics, electric vehicle powertrains and consumer grade appliances.
